.TH FERRY 1 "2026-08-01" "ferry 0.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferry \- keep a NAS folder and OneDrive as a two-way mirror, safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferry
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ferry
wraps
.BR "rclone bisync" (1)
in the safety rails a two-way mirror of real data needs, and hides the flags
behind a handful of commands. It is configured once per machine with
.B ferry setup
and thereafter runs unattended under
.BR launchd .
.PP
The NAS side is Path1 and is treated as primary: it is the side that wins by
default when the pair has to be re-established. OneDrive is Path2.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Guided setup. Finds or creates the rclone remotes, asks which folders pair with
each other, writes the config file, then runs
.BR doctor .
Run this first on a new Mac.
.TP
.B markers
Place the
.B RCLONE_TEST
marker files that
.B \-\-check\-access
requires, one on each side. Shows the top-level entry count of both sides first
so an empty or half-mounted share is visible before anything is written. Needs a
terminal unless
.B \-\-yes
is given.
.TP
.B doctor
Check every precondition: rclone present and new enough, remotes configured and
reachable, markers in place, attic not overlapping the synced tree, cloud
headroom, and whether the pair is established or blocked. Exits non-zero if
anything fails.
.TP
.B check
Compare both sides with
.BR "rclone check" .
Read-only.
.TP
.BI sync " [\-n] [\-v]"
The real run, and what the schedule invokes. Refuses to run if the pair is
blocked or was never established. Takes a lock so runs cannot stack up.
.B \-n
previews without changing anything.
.TP
.BI status " [\-\-porcelain]"
Last run and its outcome, whether a run is in progress, whether the pair is
blocked, and whether the launchd job is loaded.
.IP
.B \-\-porcelain
writes machine-readable
.I key=value
lines to standard output instead, leaving the human report on standard error.
The key
.I state
is the single field describing overall health, one of
.BR syncing ", " blocked ", " unestablished ", " never ", " failed ", " stale " or " ok ,
in that order of precedence. This is a stable interface; the human report is not.
.TP
.BI resync " [\-n] [\-\-mode " mode "] [\-\-yes]"
Establish or re-establish the pair. This is a decision about which side is
truth, so it refuses to run without a terminal unless
.B \-\-yes
is passed.
.I mode
is one of
.BR path1 " (default, the NAS wins), " path2 ", " newer ", " older ", " larger ", " smaller .
.TP
.B attic list|restore \fIDATE\fR [\fIDEST\fR]|prune
Inspect, recover from, or prune the attic of deleted and overwritten files.
.TP
.B schedule install|remove|status
Manage the launchd job.
.TP
.B app install|remove|status
Manage Ferry.app, the native menu bar indicator. The app is a thin shell over
this script: it renders
.B status \-\-porcelain
and shells out for actions, keeping all logic in one place. It never syncs on
its own timer (launchd owns the schedule) and never touches the network.
.B install
copies the bundle into
.IR ~/Applications ,
offers login registration, and removes the retired SwiftBar plugin if one is
found so two indicators never coexist.
.TP
.BI uninstall " [\-\-purge] [\-\-yes]"
Remove the launchd agent and the menu bar plugin. Run this
.B before
.BR "brew uninstall ferry" :
Homebrew formulae have no uninstall hook \(em that is a cask-only feature \(em
so an orphaned agent would otherwise go on retrying a deleted binary every
.I INTERVAL
indefinitely.
.IP
Configuration and state are kept by default.
.B \-\-purge
deletes those too, which discards the bisync listings: the pair could then only
be re-established by a full resync, resurrecting any deletion made in the
meantime. It refuses to run without a terminal unless
.B \-\-yes
is passed.
.TP
.BI activity " [\-n " N "] [\-\-porcelain]"
Recent per-file transfers, parsed from the run logs \(em nothing is recorded
beyond what rclone already logs. Newest first, default 50.
.B \-\-porcelain
emits TAB-separated records:
.IR epoch ", " action ", " path .
.TP
.BI config\-set " KEY VALUE"
Write one setting to the config file, validated exactly as
.B ferry
itself would validate it \(em unknown keys, non-numeric values for numeric
keys, and an attic inside the synced tree are all rejected. Used by
Ferry.app's settings window; equally usable from scripts.
.TP
.B remotes|remote\-create\-smb|remote\-create\-onedrive|browse|mkdir|peek
Primitives behind Ferry.app's onboarding, equally usable from scripts:
list configured rclone remotes, create an SMB remote (password on stdin),
create a OneDrive remote from an authorize token (token on stdin; without
.B \-\-drive
it lists the account's drives as TSV and exits 2), list a path's
subdirectories, create a folder, and count a path's top-level entries.
Nothing assumes a provider or a name.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B ferry
reads
.I ~/.config/ferry/config
as
.IR KEY=value ,
one per line. It is parsed, not sourced: an unrecognised key is an error rather
than a silent no-op. Override the location with
.BR FERRY_CONFIG .
.TP
.B PATH1
The NAS side. Default
.IR unas-vault:Vault .
.TP
.B PATH2
The cloud side. Default
.IR onedrive: .
.TP
.B ATTIC
Where files deleted or overwritten on Path1 are kept.
.B Must not be inside PATH1
\(em an attic inside the synced tree would sync itself to the cloud and
resurrect every deletion. Default
.IR unas-vault:ferry-attic .
.TP
.B MAX_DELETE
Abort the run if more than this
.B percentage
of files would be deleted. Default 5. rclone's own default is 50.
.TP
.B ATTIC_KEEP_DAYS
Dated attic directories older than this are purged after a successful run.
Default 90.
.TP
.B INTERVAL
Seconds between scheduled runs. Default 14400 (four hours).
.TP
.B TRANSFERS ", " CHECKERS ", " TPSLIMIT ", " RETRIES ", " LOW_LEVEL_RETRIES
Passed through to rclone. Defaults 8, 16, 10, 3, 10.
.TP
.B LOG_KEEP
Number of run logs retained. Default 30.
.TP
.B NOTIFY
1 to post a macOS notification when a run fails. Default 1.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ferry/config
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ferry/workdir
bisync's saved listings. Deliberately not rclone's default of
.IR ~/Library/Caches ,
which macOS may purge \(em losing these forces a full
.BR resync .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ferry/logs
One log per run, plus launchd's stdout and stderr.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ferry/blocked
Present when the pair needs a human decision. Its contents explain why.
.TP
.I ~/Applications/Ferry.app
The menu bar indicator, when installed.
.TP
.I ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.stphung.ferry.plist
The schedule.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 1 for a usage or precondition failure. Otherwise rclone's own
exit status is passed through.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rclone (1),
.BR salvage (1)
.PP
https://rclone.org/bisync/ \(em read the Limitations section before trusting a
two-way mirror with data you cannot lose.
